Phase 1 – Build a Static Knowledge Model

Parse repositories into a normalized model.

{
  "controllers": [],
  "services": [],
  "entities": [],
  "repositories": [],
  "databaseTables": [],
  "apiEndpoints": [],
  "kafkaTopics": [],
  "rabbitQueues": [],
  "featureFlags": [],
  "configuration": [],
  "businessRules": [],
  "tests": []
}

Most of this can be extracted using language-specific parsers (JavaParser, Roslyn, Tree-sitter, etc.) without executing code.

⸻

Phase 2 – Link Stories to Code

Avoid manual mapping whenever possible. Build links using multiple signals:

Signal	Confidence
JIRA ID in commit message	100%
JIRA ID in PR title	100%
Branch name contains story	95%
Commit references story	95%
Files modified after story creation	80%
AI semantic match	70%

The result is a candidate set of files likely related to the story.

⸻

Phase 3 – Build an Evidence Graph

Rather than storing raw files, build a graph such as:

Story
